Quick Checklist for Each Repo
When you create a repo, GitHub will ask:

Repository name: (e.g., web, core, infra, docs)

Description: Use these:

web: "Next.js frontend for Qordi (voice-to-insight companion)"
core: "Shared business logic (skills, models, utilities)"
infra: "OpenClaw VPS setup, Docker configs, deployment"
docs: "Architecture, decisions, roadmap, specifications"
Public or Private?: Choose Public (builds credibility, easier to share)

Add .gitignore: Select Node (since you're using Node)

Add README.md: Check the box ✅

